5,Okpela language — Grokipedia,https://grokipedia.com/page/okpela_language,"Okpella, also known as Ivbie North-Okpela-Arhe (ISO 639-3: atg), is an Edoid language spoken by the Okpella people in north-central Edo State, Nigeria, approximately 120 kilometers north of Benin City. [1][2] It is classified within the North Edoid subgroup of the Volta-Niger branch of the Niger-Congo language family and is considered a dialect cluster that includes varieties such as ...",Ivbie North-Okpela-Arhe,Niger-Congo
